<title>USA: Moyco sued by Cabot Corp.</title>
<headline>Moyco sued by Cabot Corp.</headline>
<dateline>MONTGOMERYVILLE, Pa. 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moyco Technologies Inc said Thursday it was served with a complaint for patent infringement.</p>
<p>The company said the complaint was filed in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California by Cabot Corp, a maker of chemical products. Moyco said the complaint alleges that a CMP slurry manufactured by Moyco infringes a U.S. patent owned by Cabot.  </p>
<p>Moyco denied that its CMP slurry products infringe on the patented Cabot product and said it retained counsel to defend against the Cabot complaint.</p>
</text>
